      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "$\\frac{a+b}{7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The denominator can be factored as the difference of squares: \n\n$$\n7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}=7({a}^{2}-{b}^{2})=7(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a+b}{7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}} & =\\frac{a+b}{7(a+b)(a-b)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(a+b)}}{7\\cancel{(a+b)}(a-b)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7(a-b)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
